<p>That level of desperate. That's what this thing was to the Serpent's Hand.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>But it's just a dog!</strong></p>
<p>I mean, can it teleport through walls? If so, how did the Hand operative even keep it in that goddamn container!? And if it can, why is it Safe and not Euclid.</p>
<p>Seriously you guys <em>it's just a dog</em>.</p>
<p>Also any way you cut it, the suicide thing is bullshit, especially if the Hand is concerned about losing more members. Which they're seriously NOT concerned about, since there was no one forcing them to feed people to the dog. They just thought that would be a cool idea I guess. Which is <em>extremely</em> contrived.</p>
<p>And so are the containment procedures, now that I think about it, since the Foundation is feeding 'just anyone' to the skip for no reason except to stop its rage stage. Why do we even care about stopping its rage state. This thing is Safe! What is it going to do, bark and gnaw at the mental container it's in? It's not like it can change the container to cardboard with its bite (which might actually be interesting).</p>
<p>edit: or teleport out, for that matter, which some people assumed was implied already by the article (but isn't actually in there).</p>
<p>(btw, a nitpick, shouldn't the cardboard bite thing just be in the Description, with a better explanation?)</p>
<p>Man this gets more hinky the more I think about it. :( Oh well.</p>

